    "source": "hn",
    "title": "Show HN: A terminal-native idle factory game, written in Rust with ratatui",
    "points": 3,
    "num_comments": 0,
    "url": "https://gitlab.com/snipedbywifi/terminactory",
    "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50497132",
    "created_at": "2026-11-14T14:05:54+00:00",
    "story_text": "Hey HN readers!<p>I&#x27;m snipedbywifi (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitlab.com&#x2F;snipedbywifi\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitlab.com&#x2F;snipedbywifi</a>), and i&#x27;ve been working on terminactory. Please try it out if you&#x27;d like to play a cozy factory game while waiting for long agent tasks to finish!<p>The game is a factory game (overused niche, i know xD), but runs in your terminal. Reason i built it? glad you asked: So basically, it started off with me wanting a terminal-native factory game. Me and the modern 5.5 claude models made a base for the game that I liked, and then i went ham adding features &#x2F; fixing some minor flaws (like adding claude code hooks so you recieve &quot;telegrams&quot; [the agent&#x27;s responses], so you can review progress directly in-game). (yes, I had heavy AI assistance, disclaimer!!!)<p>Right now, the game has basic factory features you&#x27;d expect from a game like this (build stuff, delete stuff, measure how much you&#x27;re earning, basic selection tools), along with a few more.. &quot;unexpected&quot; features. This includes a fake in-game browser that has a wiki, fake forums, some fun bits of lore, some more lore, a LOT more lore, and a research graph that shows how many items or how much RP (research points) you&#x27;d need to unlock something, and some more QOL features.<p>If anyone actually has this issue &#x2F; want of a terminal-based game that runs alongside your agents so you don&#x27;t doomscroll, do you have any suggestions, or additional ideas I could add?<p>It&#x27;s hosted on GitLab, soo, that&#x27;s one additional thing i&#x27;d like to mention<p>Thanks for reading!! snipedbywifi<p>(p.s. first HN post lol)\n(p.s. p.s. there&#x27;s a lot of hidden lore in the game, so.. lore-divers? you might like it?)",
    "matched_keywords": []
  },
